WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.330
Article 2, paragraph 4 of the UN
Charter sets a rule for every member.

2
00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:10.970
States must not use force against the
territorial integrity or political independence

3
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.910
of any state.

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:16.830
Yet states still intervene
with force in other states.

5
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:20.030
Do they act only when the
Security Council gives permission?

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.010
Or for other reasons?

7
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.410
So if states promise never to
use force against each other,

8
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:29.310
why do they still
intervene, and at what cost?

9
00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:33.950
In this mission, you'll map the rule, and
the exceptions that let states use force

10
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.310
lawfully.

11
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.830
Then you'll follow real interventions,
from the reasons states gave to what they

12
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.870
cost.

13
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.630
Your mission: explain why states
still intervene with force,

14
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.920
and evaluate what it costs.
